4,3|receive: rqn size packets bytes
The IO app is receiving packets from the receive queue.

'rqn' is the receive queue identifer.
'size' is the size of the queue.
'packets' is the number of packets receivable from the queue.
'bytes' is the number of bytes receivable from the queue.

4,9|out_of_buffer: rqn packets
The ConnectX app has synchronized receive queue drop statistics.
In ConnectX terminology, we drop packets when have no available receive 
queue buffers at the time of arrival, i.e. we are "out of buffers".

'rqn' is the receive queue identifer.
'packets' is the number of packets dropped since the last event.

4,9|rxstats: bytes packets mcast bcast drop errors
The ConnectX app has synchronized receive statistics.

'bytes' is the total number of bytes received.
'packets' is the total number of packets received.
'mcast' is the total number of multicast packets received.
'bcast' is the total number of broadcast packets received.
'drop' is the total number of packets dropped.
'errors' is the total number of receive errors.
